# How loud is loud?
subtitle: "Rank five sounds from a whisper to a jet, then see why ten decibels more means ten times the energy, and when loud starts to harm."
voices: {"a":"gemini:Iapetus | a clear, curious quiz host; plain and friendly","take":"lines"}
format: quiz

## How loud is loud?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: cdc
      title: What noises cause hearing loss?
      authors: US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention
      year: 2024
      url: https://www.cdc.gov/hearing-loss/causes/
      finding: normal conversation 60-70 dBA; long or repeated exposure at or above 85 dBA can cause hearing loss; fireworks 140-160 dBA

    cards sounds cites ["cdc"] size 1.3 y 580 ends ["loudest","quietest"] hidden true
        * "Jet take-off" icon.of "airplane departure" icon.set twemoji
        * "Rock concert" icon.of guitar icon.set twemoji
        * "Lawnmower" icon ["lawn mower","mower","tractor"]
        * "Conversation" icon.of "speech balloon" icon.set twemoji
        * "Whisper" icon.of "shushing face" icon.set twemoji
    shape bar1 #2f6b8f shape rect x 180 y 288.5 width 90 height 217 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35 hidden true
    text db1 "140 dB" #2f6b8f x 180 y 425 font_size 36 hidden true
    shape bar2 #2f6b8f shape rect x 340 y 265.25 width 90 height 170.5 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35 hidden true
    text db2 "110 dB" #2f6b8f x 340 y 378.5 font_size 36 hidden true
    shape bar3 #2f6b8f shape rect x 500 y 249.75 width 90 height 139.5 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35 hidden true
    text db3 "90 dB" #2f6b8f x 500 y 347.5 font_size 36 hidden true
    shape bar4 #2f6b8f shape rect x 660 y 226.5 width 90 height 93 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35 hidden true
    text db4 "60 dB" #2f6b8f x 660 y 301 font_size 36 hidden true
    shape bar5 #2f6b8f shape rect x 820 y 203.25 width 90 height 46.5 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35 hidden true
    text db5 "30 dB" #2f6b8f x 820 y 254.5 font_size 36 hidden true
    text rule "+10 dB = 10× energy" #b5482e x 640 y 470 font_size 44 hidden true
    text k1000 "chat = 1,000× whisper" #b5482e x 640 y 470 font_size 40 hidden true
    shape sq_big #b5482e shape rect x 560 y 305 width 230 height 230 style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35 hidden true
    shape sq_small #2f6b8f shape rect x 250 y 340 width 4 height 4 style.fill #2f6b8f hidden true
    text l_big "concert" #b5482e x 830 y 390 font_size 40 hidden true
    text l_small "chat" #2f6b8f x 250 y 295 font_size 34 hidden true
    text k100k "100,000×" #b5482e x 830 y 300 font_size 52 hidden true
    text k2 "≈ 2× as loud" #8f887c x 260 y 215 font_size 36 hidden true
    text k85 "85 dB+: hearing risk" #b5482e x 250 y 215 font_size 34 hidden true
    ellipse chat_ring #2f6b8f x 250 y 340 rx 16 ry 16 hidden true
    icon ear size 60 set twemoji x 110 y 215 icon_look picture of ear hidden true

    card title "How loud is loud?"

How loud is loud? Here are five everyday sounds.
    draw sounds

    ask "Put these sounds in order, from the loudest to the quietest: drag the cards, then press Answer." on sounds store r
        right: From the top: the jet, the concert, the mower, a chat, and a whisper.
        wrong: You got {r}.

Sound is measured in decibels. A whisper is about thirty, a conversation about sixty.
    draw bar5 bar4 db5 db4

A lawnmower is around ninety.
    draw bar3 db3

A rock concert is about a hundred and ten, and a jet taking off nearby, about a hundred and forty.
    draw bar2 bar1 db2 db1

But a decibel is not like a centimetre: every ten decibels means ten times the sound energy.
    draw rule

    erase rule

So a conversation carries a thousand times the energy of a whisper.
    draw k1000

    erase k1000 bar1 bar2 bar3 bar4 bar5 db1 db2 db3 db4 db5

And a rock concert, fifty decibels louder than a chat, carries a hundred thousand times as much.
    draw sq_small chat_ring l_small sq_big l_big k100k

Your ears soften the bl (@draw ear k2@)ow: each ten decibels only sounds about twice as loud.

    erase k2 ear

So it is easy to forget that  (@draw k85@)long hours above eighty-five decibels can harm your hearing for good.

Earplugs at the next concert are not a bad idea.
    highlight sounds_2
---
